# Prepares the built fixture orc-priest-pain-seed1-sneakopts for the checks that load it (bd inc-10v7f).
# The old fixture, a .sav, held this state (bd inc-b4l3g.2, tools/check_feed_upon_pain.sh): wizard mode on; the
# priest wounded; one punch thrown, so he carries a Feed upon Pain tally; every monster gone.
# WOUNDED: a summoned giant rat bites while the priest waits. The wait is cut short while a hostile is in view,
# so many waits are sent. THE PUNCH: the priest brawls (empty weapon hand) and punches the rat once.
# The caller exports INCURSION_LOF_FORCE_ROLL and INCURSION_FORCE_DAMAGE_ROLL for the run (the check sets 20 and
# 3 for the priest case: the rat then bites for a known amount and the punch deals a known 6, the tally).
# Ruling V7-1: a fixture holds only the created character, so the checks that need the state make it here.
@while "more --" SPACE
w
@while "Enter wizard mode" y
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
ESC

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Animals"
@choose "giant rat"
RIGHT ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC
. . . . . . . . . .
. . . . . . . . . .
. . . . .
RIGHT
@while "Die?" n

w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
s
